I couldn't inspect the tree from this chat (no file-system tool available here), so let me state the fix and drop the reusable logic in a small util you can point me at the right place for.

## The problem

`.ts` really is ambiguous: it is **TypeScript** *and* **MPEG‑TS** (transport stream). Same story for `m4a/aac/opus/sub`. So extension-only routing will always mis-render some files.

## The rule to apply

1. **Sniff the first ~1 KB of content** (magic numbers) before choosing a media preview.
2. **Only keep audio/video preview for well-known formats** (mp4, m4v, mov, webm, ogv / mp3, m4a, aac, wav, ogg, oga, flac, opus) — drop `ts`, `mts`, `m2ts`, `mkv`, `avi`, `sub` from the “preview” lists.
3. **Fallback = text mode**, with the extension still driving syntax highlighting, so `.ts` renders as TypeScript unless the bytes really are a transport stream (`0x47` sync byte every 188 bytes — a TS source file never matches 3 consecutive packets).

After sniffing, if no media signature matches → `text`.

<file_change path="src/app/shared/file-type.util.ts" language="typescript" change_type="new" encoding="text">
/**
 * File type detection helpers shared by the file viewer.
 *
 * The extension alone is not a reliable source of truth: `.ts` is both
 * TypeScript and MPEG transport stream, `.m4a` / `.aac` / `.opus` are shared
 * with other formats, etc. The rule applied by the viewer is:
 *
 *  1. Images and PDF are resolved by extension (unambiguous).
 *  2. Audio / video preview is only used for the most standard, well known
 *     formats, and always after sniffing the file header (magic numbers).
 *  3. Anything that does not match a known media signature falls back to text
 *     mode, keeping the extension for syntax highlighting (so `.ts` renders as
 *     TypeScript unless the content really is a transport stream).
 */

export type FileViewMode = 'image' | 'audio' | 'video' | 'pdf' | 'text';

/** Extensions previewed as image / pdf without sniffing. */
export const IMAGE_EXTENSIONS = [
  'png', 'jpg', 'jpeg', 'gif', 'webp', 'bmp', 'svg', 'ico', 'avif',
];
export const PDF_EXTENSIONS = ['pdf'];

/**
 * "Standard" media extensions: only these get an audio / video preview when no
 * content sample is available. `ts`, `mts`, `m2ts`, `mkv`, `avi`, `sub`... are
 * deliberately excluded (unsupported by the browser and/or ambiguous).
 */
export const AUDIO_EXTENSIONS = [
  'mp3', 'wav', 'ogg', 'oga', 'flac', 'm4a', 'aac', 'opus', 'weba',
];
export const VIDEO_EXTENSIONS = ['mp4', 'm4v', 'mov', 'webm', 'ogv'];

/** Mime types used by the `<audio>` / `<video>` source element. */
export const MEDIA_MIME_TYPES: Record<string, string> = {
  mp3: 'audio/mpeg',
  wav: 'audio/wav',
  ogg: 'audio/ogg',
  oga: 'audio/ogg',
  flac: 'audio/flac',
  m4a: 'audio/mp4',
  aac: 'audio/aac',
  opus: 'audio/ogg; codecs=opus',
  weba: 'audio/webm',
  mp4: 'video/mp4',
  m4v: 'video/mp4',
  mov: 'video/quicktime',
  webm: 'video/webm',
  ogv: 'video/ogg',
};

/** Number of leading bytes needed to detect every supported signature. */
export const SNIFF_SAMPLE_SIZE = 1024;

export function getExtension(fileName: string): string {
  const name = (fileName || '').split(/[?#]/)[0];
  const slash = name.lastIndexOf('/');
  const base = slash >= 0 ? name.slice(slash + 1) : name;
  const dot = base.lastIndexOf('.');
  if (dot <= 0 || dot === base.length - 1) {
    return '';
  }
  return base.slice(dot + 1).toLowerCase();
}

function bytesStartWith(bytes: Uint8Array, text: string, offset = 0): boolean {
  if (bytes.length < offset + text.length) {
    return false;
  }
  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {
    if (bytes[offset + i] !== text.charCodeAt(i)) {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

function bytesEqual(bytes: Uint8Array, offset: number, signature: number[]): boolean {
  if (bytes.length < offset + signature.length) {
    return false;
  }
  return signature.every((value, index) => bytes[offset + index] === value);
}

function asciiAt(bytes: Uint8Array, offset: number, length: number): string {
  let text = '';
  for (let i = offset; i < Math.min(offset + length, bytes.length); i++) {
    text += String.fromCharCode(bytes[i]);
  }
  return text;
}

const FTYP_AUDIO_BRANDS = ['M4A ', 'M4B ', 'M4P ', 'f4a ', 'mp4a'];
const FTYP_VIDEO_BRANDS = [
  'isom', 'iso2', 'iso4', 'iso5', 'iso6', 'mp41', 'mp42', 'avc1',
  'M4V ', 'M4VH', 'mmp4', 'qt  ', '3gp4', '3gp5', 'dash',
];

/**
 * MPEG transport streams start with 0x47 ('G') and repeat it every 188 bytes.
 * Requiring three synchronized packets keeps `.ts` source files (which may
 * start with 'G') from being detected as video.
 */
function isMpegTransportStream(bytes: Uint8Array): boolean {
  const packetSize = 188;
  const packets = 3;
  if (bytes.length < packetSize * packets) {
    return false;
  }
  for (let i = 0; i < packets; i++) {
    if (bytes[i * packetSize] !== 0x47) {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

/** True when the sample looks like decodable text (no NUL, few control chars). */
export function looksLikeText(bytes: Uint8Array): boolean {
  if (!bytes.length) {
    return true;
  }
  let control = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < bytes.length; i++) {
    const byte = bytes[i];
    if (byte === 0) {
      return false;
    }
    const isAllowedControl = byte === 0x09 || byte === 0x0a || byte === 0x0d || byte === 0x0c || byte === 0x1b;
    if (byte < 0x20 && !isAllowedControl) {
      control++;
    }
  }
  return control / bytes.length < 0.02;
}

/**
 * Detects the media kind from the first bytes of the file.
 * Returns null when the content does not match any known media signature.
 */
export function sniffMediaKind(bytes: Uint8Array | null | undefined): FileViewMode | null {
  if (!bytes || bytes.length < 4) {
    return null;
  }

  // Images
  if (bytesEqual(bytes, 0, [0x89, 0x50, 0x4e, 0x47])) {
    return 'image'; // png
  }
  if (bytesEqual(bytes, 0, [0xff, 0xd8, 0xff])) {
    return 'image'; // jpeg
  }
  if (bytesStartWith(bytes, 'GIF8') || bytesStartWith(bytes, 'BM') || bytesStartWith(bytes, 'II*\u0000')) {
    return 'image'; // gif / bmp / tiff
  }
  if (bytes.length > 12 && bytesStartWith(bytes, 'RIFF') && bytesStartWith(bytes, 'WEBP', 8)) {
    return 'image';
  }

  // Documents
  if (bytesStartWith(bytes, '%PDF')) {
    return 'pdf';
  }

  // ISO base media (mp4 / m4a / mov / m4v / 3gp)
  if (bytesStartWith(bytes, 'ftyp', 4)) {
    const brand = asciiAt(bytes, 8, 4);
    if (FTYP_AUDIO_BRANDS.includes(brand)) {
      return 'audio';
    }
    if (FTYP_VIDEO_BRANDS.includes(brand)) {
      return 'video';
    }
    return 'video';
  }

  // Matroska / WebM
  if (bytesEqual(bytes, 0, [0x1a, 0x45, 0xdf, 0xa3])) {
    return 'video';
  }
  // Ogg (audio or video, audio preview is the safe default)
  if (bytesStartWith(bytes, 'OggS')) {
    return 'audio';
  }
  // WAV / AVI (both RIFF containers)
  if (bytesStartWith(bytes, 'RIFF') && bytesStartWith(bytes, 'WAVE', 8)) {
    return 'audio';
  }
  if (bytesStartWith(bytes, 'RIFF') && bytesStartWith(bytes, 'AVI ', 8)) {
    return 'video';
  }
  // FLAC
  if (bytesStartWith(bytes, 'fLaC')) {
    return 'audio';
  }
  // MP3 (ID3 tag or raw frame sync) and ADTS AAC
  if (bytesStartWith(bytes, 'ID3')) {
    return 'audio';
  }
  if (bytes.length > 1 && bytes[0] === 0xff && (bytes[1] & 0xe0) === 0xe0) {
    return 'audio';
  }
  // MPEG transport stream (.ts / .m2ts ...) must be confirmed by its sync bytes
  if (isMpegTransportStream(bytes)) {
    return 'video';
  }

  return null;
}

/**
 * Resolves how a file must be rendered.
 *
 * @param fileName file name (used for the extension and syntax highlighting)
 * @param sample   first bytes of the file content, when already available
 */
export function resolveViewMode(fileName: string, sample?: Uint8Array | null): FileViewMode {
  const extension = getExtension(fileName);

  if (IMAGE_EXTENSIONS.includes(extension)) {
    return 'image';
  }
  if (PDF_EXTENSIONS.includes(extension)) {
    return 'pdf';
  }

  const sniffed = sniffMediaKind(sample);
  if (sniffed && sniffed !== 'pdf') {
    return sniffed;
  }
  if (sniffed === 'pdf') {
    return 'pdf';
  }

  // Content available but no media signature: trust the content and use text
  // mode (this is what fixes `.ts` files being treated as transport streams).
  if (sample && sample.length) {
    return looksLikeText(sample) ? 'text' : 'text';
  }

  // No content to sniff: only preview unambiguous, well known media formats.
  if (VIDEO_EXTENSIONS.includes(extension)) {
    return 'video';
  }
  if (AUDIO_EXTENSIONS.includes(extension)) {
    return 'audio';
  }
  return 'text';
}

/** Reads the header sample from an already loaded blob / file. */
export async function readSampleFromBlob(blob: Blob): Promise<Uint8Array> {
  const buffer = await blob.slice(0, SNIFF_SAMPLE_SIZE).arrayBuffer();
  return new Uint8Array(buffer).slice(0, SNIFF_SAMPLE_SIZE);
}

/**
 * Reads the header sample of a remote file with a ranged request.
 * Returns null when the content cannot be fetched (caller must fall back to the
 * extension based detection).
 */
export async function readSampleFromUrl(url: string): Promise<Uint8Array | null> {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(url, {
      headers: { Range: `bytes=0-${SNIFF_SAMPLE_SIZE - 1}` },
    });
    if (!response.ok && response.status !== 206) {
      return null;
    }
    const buffer = await response.arrayBuffer();
    return new Uint8Array(buffer).slice(0, SNIFF_SAMPLE_SIZE);
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
</file_change>

## Wiring in the file viewer

- Replace the current `isAudio(fileName) / isVideo(fileName)` extension checks with `resolveViewMode(fileName, sample)`.
- Load the sample once per selected file (`readSampleFromBlob` for local/attachment files, `readSampleFromUrl` for remote ones) before/alongside loading the preview.
- `viewMode === 'text'` → your code editor/markdown renderer using `getExtension(fileName)` for the language id (`ts` → `typescript`).
- `audio`/`video` → `<audio|video>` with `MEDIA_MIME_TYPES[extension]` as source `type`.

If you tell me the exact component path (`…/file-viewer.component.ts` — I assumed an app layout under `src/app`), I'll apply the integration itself instead of only adding the util.

