I'll start by locating the actual FileViewer component in the project so the util gets wired in correctly.Stored the content-sniffing rule for the viewer. Now the component itself.

<file_change path="src/app/components/FileViewer.vue" language="vue" change_type="update" encoding="text">
<script setup>
import {
  MEDIA_MIME_TYPES,
  SNIFF_SAMPLE_SIZE,
  getExtension,
  readSampleFromBlob,
  readSampleFromUrl,
  resolveViewMode
} from '@/app/shared/file-type.util'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex flex-col bg-[#1a1a1a] border border-white/5 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/[0.02]">
      <i class="fas fa-file text-white/30 text-xs"></i>
      <span class="text-sm text-white/80 truncate flex-1" :title="fileName">{{ fileName }}</span>
      <span class="badge badge-sm border-white/10 bg-white/5 text-white/50 font-mono">
        {{ extension || 'file' }}
      </span>
      <span :class="modeBadgeClass">
        <span :class="modeDotClass"></span>
        {{ modeLabel }}
      </span>
    </div>

    <!-- Loading -->
    <div v-if="loading" class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 py-16 text-white/40">
      <span class="loading loading-spinner loading-md text-primary"></span>
      <span class="text-xs">Loading preview…</span>
    </div>

    <!-- Error -->
    <div v-else-if="error" class="m-4 alert border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/10 text-red-300 rounded-lg">
      <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation text-sm"></i>
      <span class="text-xs">{{ error }}</span>
    </div>

    <!-- Preview -->
    <div v-else class="min-h-0" :style="{ maxHeight: maxHeight, overflow: 'auto' }">

      <!-- Image -->
      <img
        v-if="viewMode === 'image'"
        :src="mediaSrc"
        :alt="`Preview of ${fileName}`"
        class="block max-w-full max-h-full mx-auto object-contain"
      />

      <!-- PDF -->
      <iframe
        v-else-if="viewMode === 'pdf'"
        :src="mediaSrc"
        :title="`Preview of ${fileName}`"
        class="block w-full border-0 bg-[#111111]"
        :style="{ height: maxHeight }"
      ></iframe>

      <!-- Audio -->
      <div v-else-if="viewMode === 'audio'" class="flex flex-col gap-3 p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary/15 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
            <i class="fas fa-music text-primary text-sm"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <p class="text-sm text-white/80 truncate">{{ fileName }}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-white/40">{{ mimeType || 'audio' }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <audio class="w-full" controls preload="metadata" :src="mediaSrc">
          Your browser does not support audio playback for {{ mimeType || fileName }}.
        </audio>
      </div>

      <!-- Video -->
      <div v-else-if="viewMode === 'video'" class="p-4">
        <video
          class="w-full rounded-lg bg-black"
          controls
          preload="metadata"
          :src="mediaSrc"
          :style="{ maxHeight: maxHeight }"
        >
          Your browser does not support video playback for {{ mimeType || fileName }}.
        </video>
      </div>

      <!-- Text (default): extension still drives syntax highlighting -->
      <pre
        v-else
        class="m-0 px-4 py-3 text-[13px] leading-6 text-white/80 font-mono whitespace-pre overflow-auto"
        :data-language="language"
      ><code>{{ textContent }}</code></pre>

    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    fileName: { type: String, required: true },
    url: { type: String, default: '' },
    blob: { type: Object, default: null },
    content: { type: String, default: null },
    maxHeight: { type: String, default: '70vh' }
  },
  data() {
    return {
      viewMode: 'text',
      textContent: '',
      blobUrl: '',
      loading: false,
      error: ''
    }
  },
  computed: {
    extension() {
      return getExtension(this.fileName)
    },
    mimeType() {
      return MEDIA_MIME_TYPES[this.extension] || ''
    },
    mediaSrc() {
      return this.blobUrl || this.url
    },
    language() {
      const aliases = { ts: 'typescript', js: 'javascript', md: 'markdown', yml: 'yaml', sh: 'bash' }
      return aliases[this.extension] || this.extension || 'plaintext'
    },
    modeLabel() {
      const labels = { image: 'Image', audio: 'Audio', video: 'Video', pdf: 'PDF', text: this.language }
      return labels[this.viewMode] || 'Text'
    },
    modeBadgeClass() {
      const base = 'badge badge-sm gap-1.5 font-medium'
      if (this.viewMode === 'text') {
        return `${base} border-white/10 bg-white/5 text-white/50`
      }
      return `${base} border-primary/30 bg-primary/15 text-primary`
    },
    modeDotClass() {
      const color = this.viewMode === 'text' ? 'bg-white/40' : 'bg-primary'
      return `w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full ${color}`
    }
  },
  watch: {
    fileName() {
      this.openFile()
    },
    url() {
      this.openFile()
    }
  },
  mounted() {
    this.openFile()
  },
  beforeUnmount() {
    this.revokeBlobUrl()
  },
  methods: {
    // Resolves the preview mode from the file content, never from the extension alone
    async openFile() {
      this.revokeBlobUrl()
      this.error = ''
      this.textContent = ''
      this.viewMode = 'text'
      if (!this.fileName) {
        return
      }
      this.loading = true
      try {
        if (this.blob) {
          this.blobUrl = URL.createObjectURL(this.blob)
        }
        const sample = await this.readSample()
        this.viewMode = resolveViewMode(this.fileName, sample)
        if (this.viewMode === 'text') {
          await this.loadText()
        }
      } catch (e) {
        this.error = e && e.message ? e.message : 'Unable to load this file'
      } finally {
        this.loading = false
      }
    },
    // First bytes of the file: magic numbers beat the extension
    async readSample() {
      if (this.content !== null && this.content !== undefined) {
        return new TextEncoder().encode(String(this.content).slice(0, SNIFF_SAMPLE_SIZE))
      }
      if (this.blob) {
        return await readSampleFromBlob(this.blob)
      }
      if (this.url) {
        return await readSampleFromUrl(this.url)
      }
      return null
    },
    async loadText() {
      if (this.content !== null && this.content !== undefined) {
        this.textContent = String(this.content)
        return
      }
      if (this.blob) {
        this.textContent = await this.blob.text()
        return
      }
      if (!this.url) {
        this.textContent = ''
        return
      }
      const response = await fetch(this.url)
      if (!response.ok) {
        throw new Error(`Unable to load file (${response.status})`)
      }
      this.textContent = await response.text()
    },
    revokeBlobUrl() {
      if (this.blobUrl) {
        URL.revokeObjectURL(this.blobUrl)
        this.blobUrl = ''
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
</file_change>

## What changed

| Dimension | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Mode resolution | extension lists (`ts` → video) | `resolveViewMode(fileName, sample)` — content first |
| Ambiguous `.ts` | MPEG transport stream | TypeScript unless 3 × `0x47` sync bytes @188 |
| Media scope | many extensions | only standard: `mp4 m4v mov webm ogv` / `mp3 wav ogg oga flac m4a aac opus weba` |
| Fallback | none (blank player) | `text` mode, extension keeps syntax highlighting (`data-language`) |
| Mime for `<audio>/<video>` | guessed | `MEDIA_MIME_TYPES[extension]` |
| Blob handling | none | object URL created + revoked on file change / unmount |
| States | — | loading spinner, error `alert`, header badge showing detected mode |

## Integration steps

1. Keep `src/app/shared/file-type.util.ts` (imports at the top of the SFC).
2. Replace your current `isAudio/isVideo` extension checks with `resolveViewMode`.
3. Pass what you already have: `:file-name`, `:url` (remote), `:blob` (attachment/upload), or `:content` (already-loaded text). No caller changes needed beyond that.
4. If your viewer renders a real code editor (Monaco / CodeMirror) instead of the `<pre>`, keep it: feed it `textContent` and `language` — the branch logic is identical.
5. Adjust the import path `@/app/shared/file-type.util` to your alias if the util lives elsewhere.

## Anti-patterns to avoid

- ❌ Keeping `ts`/`m2ts`/`mkv`/`avi`/`sub` in the video list “just in case” — browsers can't decode them, you get a silent black player instead of the source code.
- ❌ Sniffing on every render — sample once per selected file (`watch` on `fileName` / `url`), not in a computed.
- ❌ Leaving `URL.createObjectURL` unrevoked; large media attachments leak memory across file switches.

## Accessibility checklist

- [x] `<img>` has `alt`, `<iframe>` has `title`, `<audio>/<video>` have text fallback children.
- [x] Mode is conveyed by **text label** (`TypeScript`, `Video`…), not color alone (badge + dot).
- [x] Native `<audio controls>` / `<video controls>` → full keyboard support for free.
- [x] Error surfaced as visible text, not only as a broken player.
- [x] Text preview keeps `font-mono` at 13px with 24px line-height for long sessions.

